\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Behold a little Child,
\par Laid in a manger bed;
\par The wintry blasts blow wild
\par Around His infant head.
\par But who is this, so lowly laid?
\par 'Tis He by whom the Worlds were made.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Alas! in what poor state
\par The Son of God is seen;
\par Why doth the Lord so great
\par Choose out a home so mean?
\par That we may learn from pride to flee,
\par And follow His humanity.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 Where Joseph plies his trade,
\par Lo! Jesus labours too;
\par The hands that all things made
\par An earthly craft pursue,
\par That weary men in Him may rest,
\par And faithful toil through Him be blest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Among the doctors see
\par The Boy so full of grace;
\par Say, wherefore taketh He
\par The scholar's lowly place?
\par That Christian boys, with reverence meet,
\par May sit and learn at Jesus' feet.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Christ, once Thyself a boy,
\par Our boyhood guard and guide;
\par Be Thou its light and joy,
\par And still with us abide,
\par That Thy dear love, so great and free,
\par May draw us evermore to Thee.
\par                                        Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
